# COMBAT SPORTS COMPARISON

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

This document defines how the Combat Athlete System (CAS) compares combat disciplines.

Every discipline possesses unique performance demands.

The purpose of this document is to describe those differences using a common framework.

This comparison enables CAS to individualize physical preparation according to the athlete's sport.

---

# Comparison Philosophy

Combat sports are not better or worse than one another.

They simply emphasize different capabilities.

CAS never compares sports to determine superiority.

CAS compares them to optimize preparation.

---

# Comparison Framework

Every discipline is evaluated across identical performance domains.

Physical.

Biomechanical.

Physiological.

Technical.

Tactical.

Psychological.

Cognitive.

Environmental.

This allows direct comparison between sports.

